file=Market Intelligence/trend/operational/principles/trend-principles.md · t·p:trend \· principles=> Universal-only.\n\n1. **Public institutional sources only** for macro (Fed / BLS / ECB / OECD / IMF / World Bank).\n2. **Every signal cites source URL + snapshot date.**\n3. **Correlation ≠ causation.** Never asserted.\n4. **Never forecast** — descriptive: "these signals exist"; not "this will happen".\n5. **Confidence tag mandatory** on emerging trends (early / gaining / mainstream).\n6. **Independence of signals** matters — 3 blogs citing each other = 1 signal.\n7. **Likelihood estimates** on regulatory horizon have confidence.\n8. **Pre-enactment ≠ enacted.** Do not conflate with `comply`'s domain.\n9. **Verification-before-completion inherited.**\n